  "analyzed_vuln": {
    "function": "dwarf_get_rnglist_offset_index_value",
    "file": "libdwarf/src/lib/libdwarf/dwarf_rnglists.c",
    "description": "Heap OOB read due to incorrect bounds check when reading an offset-table entry from .debug_rnglists. The function computes `offsetptr = con->rc_offsets_array + offsetentry_index * con->rc_offset_size`, but validates only `(con->rc_offsets_off_in_sect + offset_len) <= con->rc_past_last_rnglist_offset`, which is effectively constant for all indices and does not include `localoffset`/`offsetentry_index`. As a result, large-but-accepted `offsetentry_index` values can make `offsetptr` point past the loaded section buffer, and `READ_UNALIGNED_CK`/_dwarf_memcpy_noswap_bytes performs a 4-byte read out of bounds.",
    "conditions": "Via fuzz_rng, attacker supplies a malformed ELF with a crafted .debug_rnglists section. `dwarf_load_rnglists()` builds a context where `rc_offset_entry_count` allows iteration in the harness, but section size is insufficient for all claimed entries. The harness then calls `dwarf_get_rnglist_offset_index_value(dbg, i, e, ...)` for each `e < offset_entry_count`; for a chosen `e`, pointer arithmetic exceeds the allocated section (`elf_load_nolibelf_section` buffer), triggering ASan in memcpy during unaligned read."
  },
